%C - draw into the Raspberry Pi firmware framebuffer (HDMI)

Syntax:
%C [-w width] [-h height] [-b depth] [-n]

Options:
   -w width    Framebuffer width in pixels (default 640)
   -h height   Framebuffer height in pixels (default 480)
   -b depth    Bits per pixel to ask for: 32 (default), 24 or 16. The demo
               draws in whatever depth the firmware actually grants.
   -n          Do not wait for Enter before exiting

The framebuffer is requested from the VideoCore firmware through the
mailbox property channel; no graphics driver is involved. The resolution
must be one the attached monitor accepts.
